<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77600" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παντέλεια</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>consummation</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ π. τῆς καταφθορᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.48.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀρετῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.38
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶσα πολιτικὰ κοινωνία λύρας
				παντελῄᾳ ποτέοικεν</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Hippod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.1.94
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἀσφαλῆ τινα καὶ βεβαίαν π. ἀγαθῶν
					ἐξικόμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.106
				</span></i>
			If; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς π. διδαχθῆναι</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τύπωσιν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.34S.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριετηρικὴ π.</span>, of the
			great mysteries, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.671d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.77
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παντέλεια</span> was a Pythagorean name of
			the number <i>ten,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theol.Ar.
				63
			</span></i>.</div>
